{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1298857-which-type-of-exalted-most-captures-your-imagination","id":1298857,"title":"Which type of Exalted most captures your imagination?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-03-22T23:27:06-07:00","id":1298857,"title":"Which type of Exalted most captures your imagination?","content":"Just which kind you find most exciting to think about","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12378-fma245","name":"FMA245","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"165"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T23:36:37-07:00","id":1298862,"title":"","content":"Infernals definitely, the relationship between an infernal and his powers are unlike any other exalted. The juggling of the many different forms of power and madness the Yozi have to offer is all fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1685-looker","name":"Looker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-23T04:44:21-07:00","id":1298911,"title":"","content":"I didn't really take to the Infernals initially, but the &quot;become a world&quot; and &quot;birth your own 3rd circle demons&quot; charm lists in the Broken Winged Crane was pretty exciting. Not that I've ever had a chance to use it.<br /> <br /> For me, though, it'll have to be Sidereals. Nothing grips me like intrigue, except intrigue with otherworldly creatures thrown in. I'm also a big fan of the Martial Arts focus. Kung-fu bureaucrats are where it's at. Their charms, too! So many clever tricks. I love that Avoiding the Truth Technique forces someone not to believe you, but to believe that you're lying. Or the subtle menace in that every Sidereal who knows a &quot;nice&quot; socialise charm necessarily knows how to remove you from Fate's register of people who are destined to be loved.<br /> <br /> I had a concept (that I also didn't get to play) for a character who'd been assigned to the Convention on Forbidden Gods (which has 2 members, both of whom were assigned there as a punishment) for abusing Life Without Compunction. He got a kick out of doing wildly inappropriate things, and having them catch on. It was causing... <i>problems</i> for other sections of the Bureau of Destiny.<br /> <br /> I'm also a big fan of using them as NPCs. In the next game I run, I'm thinking of having some Gold Faction sidereals mentor the Solar PCs, and giving them all 1 solar xp per session that they continue to put up with the Sidereals' shiftiness for the sake of training.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24421-katamari_naneke","name":"Katamari_Naneke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}